I never asked for you to
come here and save me, Leo.

283
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:18,500
I put my life on the line.

284
00:15:18,660 --> 00:15:19,954
You are so ungrateful.

285
00:15:20,060 --> 00:15:22,413
Do you really want me to leave you here?

286
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:24,170
Go!

287
00:15:27,220 --> 00:15:29,040
Just carry her out for now.

288
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:30,300
We got to go.

289
00:15:31,340 --> 00:15:32,340
That hurt.

290
00:15:35,460 --> 00:15:36,780
You're obnoxious.

291
00:15:37,340 --> 00:15:40,260
Selfish, fickle, despicable,
and mean-spirited.

292
00:15:40,540 --> 00:15:42,900
Such a huge, huge pain in the patootie.

293
00:15:43,420 --> 00:15:45,320
His back feels nice.

294
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:49,300
Our princess is just the sweetest.

295
00:15:51,420 --> 00:15:53,580
How thick-headed can Leo be?

296
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:56,840
Big problem!

297
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:58,937
They took Mad Sherry and ran off!

298
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:00,760
Go after the little people!

299
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:02,257
They went that way!

300
00:16:02,340 --> 00:16:03,560
Seize them!

301
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:06,560
How embarrassing.

302
00:16:07,180 --> 00:16:11,400
I hate to admit defeat, but
the situation has become dire.

303
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:19,320
He won't be thrilled, but I
must report to the young master.

304
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:22,097
I recall him saying that Mancherry's devil

305
00:16:22,180 --> 00:16:24,651
fruit must have a hidden ultimate ability.

306
00:16:25,300 --> 00:16:29,177
He believed that he could use that if
something happened to the Smile Factory.

307
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:32,740
If she traded her life to call
forth that forbidden power,

308
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,037
she could restore it to its former glory.

309
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:37,885
Without that fail-safe,
we could be in trouble.

310
00:16:41,860 --> 00:16:46,260
If nothing is done, then
the factory is in peril.

311
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:48,200
It's on you, senor.

312
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:51,580
You're our last line of defense. Franky!

313
00:16:52,860 --> 00:16:53,690
No!

314
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:56,000
Senor, please be careful.

315
00:16:58,040 --> 00:16:59,760
Strong hammer!

316
00:17:05,860 --> 00:17:06,720
Ah!

317
00:17:06,940 --> 00:17:08,587
He dove in the ground again!

318
00:17:08,700 --> 00:17:09,600
Farland, look!

319
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:11,220
It's the attack dive!

320
00:17:12,260 --> 00:17:13,120
Dive!

321
00:17:16,780 --> 00:17:18,140
Meow meow!

322
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:19,460
Suplex!

323
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:29,180
Oh, this is Yarr!

324
00:17:41,820 --> 00:17:43,440
Senor must be at his limit.

325
00:17:44,020 --> 00:17:44,850
Froland!

326
00:17:46,260 --> 00:17:47,217
Something's wrong.

327
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:49,157
You could have easily dodged that.

328
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:50,280
What's with you?

329
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:53,794
Why'd we see you take the
same move over and over again?

330
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:57,140
Stay out of this, tontadas.

331
00:17:58,380 --> 00:18:02,197
You know, Senor's also been hit with
the same punch 30 times in a row, too.

332
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:03,960
Why would he do that?

333
00:18:04,340 --> 00:18:06,977
When someone offers to
buy a round at the bar.

334
00:18:07,060 --> 00:18:11,840
If you're a real man, then you wouldn't
dare take your glass off of the table!

335
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:14,620
You're getting hit on purpose?

336
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,817
This guy's a bro among bros.

337
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:21,380
So I'm gonna take every attack
he throws at me out of respect.

338
00:18:22,760 --> 00:18:25,057
He can throw whatever he's got at me.

339
00:18:25,140 --> 00:18:26,460
I'll still win

340
00:18:28,780 --> 00:18:31,400
We're doing it strong style, baby

341
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:35,637
It's cute that you're concerned,

342
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:38,337
but this is a man's
fight So just stand back

343
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:41,577
and watch me win don't
fret little friends.

344
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:43,880
I won't let you lose your freedom

345
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:57,900
Your words make me tipsier than
any dive bar I'd ever been to, kid.

346
00:18:59,980 --> 00:19:02,568
I'd like to see you
back up that fancy talk.

347
00:19:05,340 --> 00:19:06,300
I'll confess.

348
00:19:07,100 --> 00:19:12,060
This body's not as spry as it used to be,
so my next move is going to settle these.

349
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:15,694
How are you two going to fight
when you're so far apart?

350
00:19:16,140 --> 00:19:17,100
Signor, closer!

351
00:19:18,540 --> 00:19:22,560
Hey, pervert, are you picking
up what I'm throwing down?

352
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:26,920
You said you'd take whatever
I can hurl at you, right?

353
00:19:27,820 --> 00:19:29,996
True men don't go back on their word.

354
00:19:30,280 --> 00:19:31,820
So let's see you try.

355
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:34,740
Surviving this one!

356
00:19:40,620 --> 00:19:45,220
If you can withstand this
final blow, I'll take the loss.

357
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:50,200
I'll accept whatever attack
you wish to dish out.

358
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:53,080
Bring it on!

359
00:19:59,420 --> 00:20:01,891
He swam straight up the side of the tower!

360
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:04,925
What in the heck is that
guy gonna do up there?

361
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:12,297
That's a mean-looking sky
today, don't you think?

362
00:20:12,380 --> 00:20:19,277
But if I can keep flying, then
maybe I can see my Russian,

363
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:23,057
Russian, yeah, I'd like to see my son.

364
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:29,297
Gimlet too, unfortunately, gravity
is going to fight me on this,

365
00:20:29,380 --> 00:20:31,337
and I can't keep flying.

366
00:20:31,420 --> 00:20:34,357
Hey, what are you rambling about?

367
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:38,077
Tell me, Cyborg, your back's
still flesh and blood, right?

368
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:39,120
Oh, damn it!

369
00:20:39,260 --> 00:20:41,180
You figured that out!

370
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:44,264
Now shut up before you
bite your own tongue off!

371
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:50,360
Meow meow suplex!

372
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:54,950
Baby...

373
00:20:57,720 --> 00:20:58,550
Buster!

374
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:18,200
Oh, my God.

375
00:21:30,900 --> 00:21:31,880
Frawl 'n!

376
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,180
Remember your words, old man.

377
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:47,020
Now you'll get to see what I'm made of.

378
00:21:50,300 --> 00:21:51,780
Oh, you got me there.

379
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:57,340
I'm sorry, young master.

380
00:21:57,560 --> 00:22:01,140
All right, Franky Iron Foxy!

381
00:22:03,680 --> 00:22:05,920
I remember now, Russian.

382
00:22:07,220 --> 00:22:11,060
The day I first met you, and
the day you stopped smiling.

383
00:22:17,520 --> 00:22:22,560
That cold dark rain kept
pouring, just like in my heart.

384
00:22:27,600 --> 00:22:29,417
It's a wet one out there, huh?

385
00:22:29,500 --> 00:22:31,057
I'm drenched.

386
00:22:31,140 --> 00:22:33,197
What's so amusing?

387
00:22:33,280 --> 00:22:35,160
Aren't you freezing cold?

388
00:22:36,200 --> 00:22:37,257
It's fine.

389
00:22:37,340 --> 00:22:38,537
I love rain.

390
00:22:38,620 --> 00:22:39,840
Feels nice.

391
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:45,577
What things don't I like?

392
00:22:45,660 --> 00:22:51,360
Oh, pirates hate him to
death, so what do you do?

393
00:22:54,860 --> 00:22:57,160
Me? I'm a... a banker.

394
00:22:58,080 --> 00:22:58,910
Oh.

395
00:23:08,040 --> 00:23:09,320
There you are.

396
00:23:11,940 --> 00:23:14,980
So, honey, what should we name him?

397
00:23:15,380 --> 00:23:17,217
He looks like...

398
00:23:17,300 --> 00:23:18,520
a Gimli.

399
00:23:19,260 --> 00:23:21,180
I think that suits him fine.

400
00:23:56,020 --> 00:23:57,457
Gimlet is dead.

401
00:23:57,540 --> 00:23:59,397
A week ago today.

402
00:23:59,480 --> 00:24:01,680
The same day you disappeared.

403
00:24:03,340 --> 00:24:05,237
He came down with a sudden fever.

404
00:24:05,320 --> 00:24:07,277
I rushed him to the hospital.

405
00:24:07,360 --> 00:24:08,654
But he didn't make it.

406
00:24:11,140 --> 00:24:12,160
You lied.

407
00:24:13,460 --> 00:24:14,497
You lied.

408
00:24:14,580 --> 00:24:17,137
I called the bank over and over.

409
00:24:17,220 --> 00:24:19,985
But they told me you were
never employed there.

410
00:24:20,660 --> 00:24:21,980
Tell me the truth!

411
00:24:22,920 --> 00:24:25,080
What do you really do for a living?

412
00:24:26,240 --> 00:24:28,840
Where did the money come from? Say it!

413
00:24:29,780 --> 00:24:30,610
Hey!

414
00:24:30,740 --> 00:24:32,240
Why won't you tell me?

415
00:24:32,500 --> 00:24:36,300
You don't have the right to
be a father anymore Move!

416
00:24:37,860 --> 00:24:38,690
Wait!

417
00:24:39,660 --> 00:24:40,940
Wait! Russian!

418
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:42,700
It's terrible out here

419
00:24:43,400 --> 00:24:45,337
You stop following me!

420
00:24:45,420 --> 00:24:47,680
I need to be alone now.

421
00:24:50,500 --> 00:24:52,600
You don't understand, Russian.

422
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:55,588
There's a reason I can't
tell you the truth.

423
00:24:56,120 --> 00:24:56,950
Russian!

424
00:24:57,320 --> 00:24:58,500
Where are you?

425
00:24:59,020 --> 00:24:59,850
Russian!

426
00:25:06,380 --> 00:25:07,780
I'm sorry to report.

427
00:25:08,140 --> 00:25:10,240
Your wife is in critical condition.

428
00:25:10,600 --> 00:25:13,600
She was trapped under a
landslide during the storm.

429
00:25:13,940 --> 00:25:15,840
She's awake, but unresponsive.

430
00:25:17,020 --> 00:25:18,500
A vegetative state?

431
00:25:19,220 --> 00:25:20,050
Exactly.

432
00:25:20,480 --> 00:25:23,117
The trauma has left her
with no signs of awareness.

433
00:25:23,200 --> 00:25:25,376
And I'm afraid she may never recover.

434
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:29,380
Sad to say, the woman you
once knew was no longer there.

435
00:25:29,860 --> 00:25:33,154
I'm not entirely sure how
much time she has left either.

436
00:25:33,280 --> 00:25:34,960
If only you hadn't met me.

437
00:25:35,160 --> 00:25:36,984
This would have never happened.

438
00:25:37,140 --> 00:25:38,940
Honey, thanks so much.

439
00:25:40,580 --> 00:25:41,437
I'm sorry.

440
00:25:41,520 --> 00:25:44,200
I didn't want to lose you.

441
00:25:44,620 --> 00:25:46,160
That's why I lied.

442
00:25:50,540 --> 00:25:53,180
I want to hear your voice.

443
00:25:55,540 --> 00:25:58,300
I want to hear you laugh.

444
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:01,660
Just once more.

445
00:26:02,140 --> 00:26:05,660
I want to see your smile.

446
00:26:06,880 --> 00:26:08,420
Just once more.

447
00:26:12,500 --> 00:26:14,020
Hey, Russian, look here!

448
00:26:14,220 --> 00:26:17,338
I found the same bonnet that
our gimlet used to wear.

449
00:26:17,920 --> 00:26:19,214
Don't I look like him?

450
00:26:19,440 --> 00:26:22,260
You used to say he had my face. I'm sorry.

451
00:26:22,840 --> 00:26:24,580
That was a poor joke.

452
00:26:24,800 --> 00:26:27,420
And just imagine if somebody saw me...

453
00:26:39,060 --> 00:26:39,890
Russian...

454
00:26:44,580 --> 00:26:45,980
Oh

455
00:27:11,520 --> 00:27:12,780
Aren't you a Kaido?

456
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:15,960
I heard he lost his son
and his wife's brain dead.

457
00:27:16,460 --> 00:27:18,600
No wonder he went off the deep end.

458
00:27:24,340 --> 00:27:25,640
What is this?

459
00:27:25,860 --> 00:27:28,566
The hell happened to
your fashion sense, Pink?

460
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:33,680
I'm heading out.

461
00:27:35,160 --> 00:27:37,020
Look, it's a weirdo.

462
00:27:37,300 --> 00:27:38,820
Keep walking, you perv.

463
00:27:39,040 --> 00:27:41,940
What a creep. Look! It's a freak!

464
00:27:42,100 --> 00:27:43,000
Hey, stop that!

465
00:27:57,900 --> 00:27:58,730
Russian.

466
00:28:02,260 --> 00:28:03,820
I look ridiculous.

467
00:28:05,260 --> 00:28:10,980
But to me, this silly outfit is
worth more than the finest suit.

468
00:28:19,080 --> 00:28:25,180
The only time you smile for me
anymore is when I wear this.

469
00:28:52,140 --> 00:28:53,760
Hang on, senor!

470
00:28:54,100 --> 00:28:56,100
Rollins, tell us that you're okay!

471
00:29:12,560 --> 00:29:14,340
You're a real mess, bro.

472
00:29:15,960 --> 00:29:18,372
What's going through your head right now?

473
00:29:19,380 --> 00:29:22,100
What's making you hurt like that?

474
00:29:41,360 --> 00:29:47,000
Tell you what, if we ever cross
paths again, let's have a round.

475
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:51,977
You can tell me all about

476
00:29:52,060 --> 00:29:55,320
that girl who goes by Russian.

477
00:29:56,040 --> 00:29:57,420
You
